Modifications for CryTerm
  Copyright (c) 2026 Danger Close Security Co.

CryTerm differs from iTerm2 in these ways:
  - Renamed to CryTerm, with its own bundle identifier
    (co.dangerclose.cryterm), so it installs and runs alongside iTerm2 with
    separate settings, saved passwords, and Application Support folder.
  - Signed and notarized by Danger Close Security Co.
  - Automatic update checks against iterm2.com are disabled.
  - Bug-report links point to the CryTerm repository.
  - iTerm2's donation prompts, sponsor logos, and patron list are removed,
    since they fund the upstream project rather than CryTerm. Please support
    iTerm2 directly at https://iterm2.com/donate.html.
  - A new app icon.
  - On first launch, offers to copy scripts, dynamic profiles, fonts, and
    ssh_config from iTerm2's Application Support folder.
  - Built for Apple silicon (arm64) only.
  - Build fixes for newer Xcode and Rust toolchains.

Every change, with its author and date, is recorded in the git history of the
source repository. The complete corresponding source code for each CryTerm
release is available at:

  https://github.com/mikemackintosh/CryTerm

under the git tag that matches the release version (for example, v3.7.0).
tools/patches/SFSymbolEnum-release-dates.patch must be applied to the
submodules/SFSymbolEnum submodule before building.

